{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]On [Bm]Jor[A]dan’s [D]bank the Bap__[A]__tist’s [D]cry
[G]An[D]nounces [A]that the [D]Lord is nigh;
[D]Come, [Bm]then, [E7]and [A7]hear[D]ken, [G]for He [D]brings
[Em]Glad [A]ti[D]dings [A]from the [G]King [A]of [D]kings.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Then [Bm]cleansed [A]be [D]every breast__[A]__ from [D]sin;
[G]Make [D]straight the [A]way for [D]God within;
[D]Pre[Bm]pare [E7]we [A7]in [D]our [G]hearts a [D]home,
[Em]Where [A]such [D]a [A]mighty [G]Guest [A]may [D]come.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]For [Bm]Thou [A]art [D]our salva__[A]__tion, [D]Lord—
[G]Our [D]refuge, [A]and our [D]great reward;
[D]With[Bm]out [E7]Thy [A7]grace, [D]our [G]souls must [D]fade
[Em]And [A]wi[D]ther [A]like a [G]flower [A]de[D]cayed.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]Stretch [Bm]forth [A]Thine [D]hand, to heal__[A]__ our [D]sore,
[G]And [D]make us [A]rise and [D]fall no more;
[D]Once [Bm]more [E7]up[A7]on [D]Thy [G]people [D]shine,
[Em]And [A]fill [D]the [A]world with [G]love [A]di[D]vine.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[D]To [Bm]Him [A]Who [D]left the throne__[A]__ of [D]Heav'n
[G]To [D]save man[A]kind, all [D]praise be giv'n;
